## Exercise 10

```typescript
enrollAll(student: Student, courses: Course[]): number {
    let accepted = 0;
    for (const course of courses) {
        if (course.isOpen()) {
            const credits = course.getCredits();
            if (student.addCredits(credits)) {
                accepted++;
            }
        }
    }
    return accepted;
}
```

## Exercise 11

| #   | Line of the diagram                                     | What is wrong                                                                                                                                                 | Correction                                                                                                                                                  |
| --- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1   | `service->>enrollment: new Enrollment(student, course)` | There is no `create participant` line before it, and the enrollment is created before the `isOpen()` check, so a closed course would still get an enrollment. | Write `create participant enrollment as enrollment: Enrollment` just before the message, and move both lines after the check, in the "course is open" path. |
| 2   | `course-->>service: true`                               | The answer can be true or false, so the return must be labelled with a question.                                                                              | `course-->>service: open?`                                                                                                                                  |
| 3   | `service->>course: seats = seats - 1`                   | This is not a call to an operation, it is a detail inside `Course`. The service must ask the course to take the seat.                                         | `service->>course: addStudent(student)`                                                                                                                     |

Corrected diagram:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant service as service: EnrollmentService
    participant course as course: Course
    User->>service: enroll(student, course)
    service->>course: isOpen()
    course-->>service: open?
    alt course is open
        service->>course: addStudent(student)
        create participant enrollment as enrollment: Enrollment
        service->>enrollment: new Enrollment(student, course)
        service-->>User: enrollment
    else course is closed
        service-->>User: undefined
    end
```
